"},"atkVal":"6","price":"2400","slot":{"zh":"武器","en":"Weapon"}},{"id":"WP1003305","name":{"zh":"铁札甲·丁","en":"Iron Lamellar Armor - IV"},"level":"1","description":{"zh":"历史悠久的甲胄，由于甲片形似书札，故称扎甲。经过几代改良，扎甲既贴身又灵活，因此各地战场皆能看到它的身影。","en":"An ancient armor type named for plates resembling writing slips. Refined over generations, lamellar armor is both form-fitting and flexible, found on battlefields everywhere."},"defenceVal":"6","mp":"180","price":"2500","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1023205","name":{"zh":"胄皮帽","en":"Leather Cap"},"level":"0","description":{"zh":"非全金属制的帽盔，与铁胄有所区别，多为临时校尉、伍长佩戴。","en":"A cap helm not made entirely of metal, distinct from iron helms, typically worn by provisional colonels and squad leaders."},"defenceVal":"1","price":"900","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}},{"id":"WP1001015","name":{"zh":"汗血","en":"Sweatblood"},"level":"2","description":{"zh":"西域进贡的纯种汗血宝马，皮肤薄，血管可见，冲刺时如流血汗。","en":"A purebred blood-sweating horse presented as tribute from the Western Regions, with thin skin and visible veins that appear to sweat blood at full gallop."},"price":"10000","slot":{"zh":"坐骑","en":"Mount"}}],"family":{"father":{"label":{"zh":"父亲","en":"Father"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1042915","code":"0"}]},"family":{"label":{"zh":"亲属","en":"Relatives"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1043715","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI113015","name":{"zh":"鲜卑拓跋氏","en":"The Tuoba clan of Xianbei"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自东胡，鲜卑族北部支系。东汉前期从大兴安岭北段南迁至呼伦贝尔草原，后继续西迁至阴山一带。三国时期鲜卑北部最强部落，北魏皇族先祖。拓跋力微在位期间吞并没鹿回部，拥有控弦之士二十余万。魏甘露三年，拓跋力微宣布承认曹魏为宗主国。其子孙在十六国时期建立代国，后发展为统一北方的北魏。","en":"Originating from the Donghu, a northern branch of the Xianbei people. In the early Eastern Han, they migrated South from the northern reaches of the Greater Khingan Mountains to the Hulunbuir Grasslands, later pressing West toward the Yin Mountains region. During the Three Kingdoms period, they stood as the most formidable Xianbei tribe in the North, serving as the imperial forebears of the Northern Wei dynasty. Under the rule of Tuoba Liwei, they annexed the Moluhui tribe, commanding over 200,000 mounted archers. In the third year of the Ganlu era of Wei, Tuoba Liwei formally acknowledged Cao Wei as suzerain. His descendants went on to establish the state of Dai during the Sixteen Kingdoms era, which eventually evolved into the Northern Wei dynasty that unified the North."},"talent":{"military":"9","commerce":"3","politics":"8"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"拓跋悉鹿","height":"平均","shape":"精壮"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1076","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role":0,"stats":[45,52,44,35,51,42],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"90","reputation":"3150","equipment":{"weapon":"WP12012","armor":"WP1003305","helmet":"WP1023205","horse":"WP1001015"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"185","month":"3"},"faction":"WJ10377","city":"CS1076","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role":0,"stats":[45,52,44,35,51,42],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"0","reputation":"3150","equipment":{"weapon":"WP12012","armor":"WP1003305","helmet":"WP1023205","horse":"WP1001015"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10615","name":{"zh":"十常侍之乱","en":"Turmoil of the Ten Attendants"},"year":"188","month":"11"},"faction":"WJ10377","city":"CS1076","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role":0,"stats":[45,52,44,35,51,42],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"80","reputation":"3400","equipment":{"weapon":"WP12012","armor":"WP1003305","helmet":"WP1023205","horse":"WP1001015"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10402","name":{"zh":"诸侯讨董","en":"Coalition Against Dong Zhuo"},"year":"190","month":"3"},"faction":"WJ10377","city":"CS1076","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role